description "Podman extras: compose and the TUI, on top of the runtime every bootc image already has"

supports "fedora" "debian" "ubuntu"

// Extras only: the runtime itself is not this module's, on any family.
// `quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc:44` ships `podman` and `crun` in the base —
// measured 2026-09-05 — and a deb base ships neither, which is what
// `deb/container-runtime` is for. So this module is what goes on top of
// a runtime that is always already there, and never the runtime.
//
// Neither `podman-machine` nor `podman-tui` exists on either deb family —
// checked 2026-09-05 — so the deb legs are the compose front end and the
// rootless networking backends.
//
// `passt` and `slirp4netns` are here for a reason `apt-cache depends podman`
// gives: deb podman only *recommends* both, and `deb/build-environment`
// installs with
// `--no-install-recommends`, so neither arrives on its own. Without one of
// them a rootless container has no network at all.
packages "podman-compose" "slirp4netns"

family "fedora" { packages "podman-machine" "podman-tui" }
family "debian" "ubuntu" { packages "passt" }
